			"Message": "refactor(Output): Apply minified build configuration and remove source maps\n\nCompress the ESBuild configuration and plugin pipeline in the Output element for reduced bundle size and faster module evaluation. Rename variables to single-character identifiers (e.g., `Editor_default` → `r`, `__name` → `d`) and collapse function bodies, while preserving all logical behavior, entry points, exclusion patterns, and plugin transforms.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Minify `Configuration/ESBuild/CodeEditorLand/Editor.js`, `Bundle.js`, and `Exclude/` scripts (Bootstrap, ChromiumIPC, Electron, Network, etc.) by removing whitespace and renaming bindings.\n- Compress `Configuration/Plugin/Apply.js`, `Copy.js`, and `Transform/` definitions (HoistFunctionDeclarations, ExposeWorkbenchAccessor, etc.) to single-line or dense block structures.\n- Minify polyfill implementations in `Configuration/Polyfill/` (ChildProcess, FileSystem, IPCRenderer, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcess) by shortening variable names and condensing control flow.\n- Update `Configuration/ESBuild/Output.js` and `Source/ESBuild/Output.js` to match the minified style.\n- Delete all `.js.map` source map files for these configurations to reflect the minified production-ready state.\n\nThe Output build pipeline remains functionally identical; only source formatting and size are affected.",
